>Yes, use BSD style partitionning.

I have a feeling ARC only understands PC style partitioning. Using
ARC you need a ~2MB FAT partition for milo at the start of the disc
preferably. For the rest try
/     250M
/var  100M
/tmp  100M
/usr  3G
/home the rest
That's six partitions so you will need an extended partition holding
three logical partitions.
Put the swap (2x RAM size) on the SCSI as well, it is twice as fast.
 
>> Well, the workstation install does not proerly find the TGA display
>> and so it doesn't work properly.

You got the X grey background. That means X is working, you just need
a window manager. Edit ~/.Xclients and add the line
exec icewm
to the end of the file. Substitute your favourite wm for icewm, and
make sure it is installed. Bear in mind KDE and Gnome will crawl on
a Multia.

Spuggy


