standard location in most PC designs. It probably is a small black plastic
container, that says Rayovac or something similar on the outside and will
have a red and black wire coming out of it and going to a header on the
board. It is usually held in place by velcroing it onto the back of some
large IC. If I had to guess for the actual location, I'd try looking for it
around the location where the serial ports and parallel port are located as
this is where the clock chip and the universal chips usually hang out.

