Pio Baettig <baettig@hotmail.com> wrote:
)Hit Ctrl-C or Ctrl-P several times during the countdown (ea..e5) it should
)halt on SRM.

When you say "several times", you need to qualify that with "repeated" and
perhaps "furious". :-)

I usually alternate CTRL-C and CTRL-P as fast as i can bang them from the
time the system is powered on until either i get SRM or the system has
decided that it doesn't like me anyway.   (<CONTROL-P> used to be a VAX
thing, but i don't think all the alpha boxen support it, or it's only
used if SRM variable "control_p = on", so that's why i do both keys)

The DUNIX boot loader traps on CTRL-C or P, so there's that little window
of opportunity, but on fast machines, that window gets very small.

Some machines have the HALT button, which will trap your machine to the
console, but i've got lots of systems that don't have HALT. :-(

FWIW, to the original poster, i find little value in using AlphaBIOS,
since aboot is pretty functional on SRM.

