The JENSEN, AKA DECpc AXP 150,

has Alpha code in firmware that is capable of initializing an Adaptec 1742.

Normally, Intel cards like display cards, and SCSI cards, get their Intel
BIOS code linked into the system BIOS at POST time and then the Intel
processor runs the Intel Code to initialize the card. The Jensen only
executes Alpha code, therfore, support is minimalist.

Later on it time, we intorduced a Intel Code emulator into Alpha's that was
loaded from SROM at POST and could execute the Intel code in the BIOS on
Display and SCSI cards. This was a thing, brought in around the time of the
AlphaServer 2100 and there on.

So, Duh.

rtt

