Hello,

  I got the same problem until I read the install docs more carefully.
Disk Druid is too stupid to install BSD-style disk label and partioning
for the Alpha in version 7.0 of RedHat.


  You have to use fdisk to partition your disk and you have to toggle
it into the bsd disklabel mode.  (b?).

  You don't *really* need to use the jumpstart CD as the other poster
has implied, if you use the bsd disklabel mode of fdisk to partition
with.  The jumpstart CD does that for you, is all.

